= The Factory Representatives

On 13 March the first assembly of authorised factory representatives met in Petrograd: delegates elected by the workers of the big factories, independent of both the soviets and the unions. They passed resolutions on bread, on unemployment, on the Cheka. The Bolsheviks were a minority. The Mensheviks, the SRs and the anarchists were not.

The movement spread to Moscow and a dozen other cities by the spring. In June it will be dispersed.

- @endorse: Endorse the assemblies, as the party did on 7 April.
- @ignore: Leave them to the workers.

@endorse
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4});
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1, repression: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 1, -1);
Q.endorsed_reps = 1;
!}

The party's Central Committee endorsed the assemblies on 7 April. A number of our members were elected as delegates, and several were arrested within the month.

@ignore
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 0, 2);
!}

We said that it was for the workers to decide. Some of our members found the answer unsatisfying.
